<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       MOVE THE ALCHEMY LINE INTO THE MEDIEVAL ERA

       The Medieval tier is the thinnest in the whole load order: 22 projects
       and 15,500 research points, against an intended 180 to 240 day era.
       At a realistic Medieval research rate (about 505 points/day with two
       pawns at Intellectual 12 on a simple bench) that is roughly 22 days of
       content. Retiering is one of three levers we have; the others are
       lifting content out of Medieval Overhaul and raising TechBlock's
       requiredPointsMedieval.

       WHY ONLY THIS CHAIN

       Nearly every Industrial project descends from Electricity, Machining
       or MicroelectronicsBasics. Retiering a project whose prerequisite
       stays Industrial achieves nothing, because the prerequisite still
       gates it. The drug line is the one substantial block that does not:
       DrugProduction has NO prerequisites at all, and the other three
       descend only from it.

       Deliberately NOT touching Machining's Electricity prerequisite, which
       would have unlocked another 5,500 points across Prosthetics,
       Gunsmithing, Mortars and friends. Conrad's call: Electricity stays
       where it is, and it remains the thing that ends the Medieval era.

       FICTION: alchemy, herbalism and opiates. Sits beside VFEM2_Alchemy,
       which is already Medieval. Nothing here needs power or machining.

       EFFECT: Medieval 15,500 -> 18,000, Industrial 147,300 -> 144,800.
       TechBlock's gate costs shift with the tier sums automatically, since
       it recomputes them from DefDatabase at startup.

       Still on the table, not done because only the drug line was approved:
       HeavyBridges (800, no prerequisites) and Piano (2000, prerequisite
       Harpsichord is already Medieval). Both are clean, zero-collateral
       moves whenever you want them.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <!-- expect: 1 -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="DrugProduction"]/techLevel</xpath>
    <value>
      <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="PsychiteRefining"]/techLevel</xpath>
    <value>
      <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="WakeUpProduction"]/techLevel</xpath>
    <value>
      <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName="GoJuiceProduction"]/techLevel</xpath>
    <value>
      <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
